; T-0015D golden: zoomify_usage_example.zmp - CP1251 source with '{...}' comments containing
; an apostrophe, user Floor/Ceil shadowing the registered builtins (Result:=Trunc(v); if v<>
; Result adjust by 1.0 - real floor/ceil for non-negative v, which every value here is), a
; procedure assigning a global (GetMaxZoom sets nMaxZoom), Trunc, IntPower, real division.
; const m_nWidth=9910; m_nHeight=7476.
; GetMaxZoom: k:=9910 (since 7476<9910); while k>256: k:=Trunc(k/2), inc(i) -> 6 iterations
; (9910->4955->2477->1238->619->309->154<=256) -> nMaxZoom:=6.
; GetTilesAtZoom(z): k:=256*IntPower(2,nMaxZoom-z); Result:=Trunc(Ceil(9910/k)*Ceil(7476/k)).
; GetTilesCount(n): sum of GetTilesAtZoom(i) for i:=0 to n-1 (0 when n<=0).
; zoom:=GetZ-1; nTileGroup := (GetX + GetY*Trunc(Ceil(9910/(256*IntPower(2,nMaxZoom-zoom)))) +
;   GetTilesCount(zoom)) div 256
; ResultURL := GetURLBase+IntToStr(nTileGroup)+'/'+IntToStr(zoom)+'-'+IntToStr(GetX)+'-'+
;   IntToStr(GetY)+'.jpg'
; All four denominators (256*2^(6-zoom)) are exact powers of two, and 9910/7476 are small, so
; every division here is EXACTLY representable in a double/Extended - no rounding-mode
; ambiguity between Delphi's 80-bit Extended and the values below.
; P1 (zoom=0): k=256*64=16384; Ceil(9910/16384)=1=mult; GetTilesCount(0)=0 (zero-trip sum);
;   nTileGroup=(0+0*1+0) div 256=0.
; P2 (zoom=1): k=256*32=8192; mult=Ceil(9910/8192)=2; GetTilesAtZoom(0): k=16384,
;   Ceil(9910/16384)*Ceil(7476/16384)=1*1=1 -> GetTilesCount(1)=1;
;   nTileGroup=(1+1*2+1) div 256=4 div 256=0.
; P3 (zoom=13): zoom is far beyond nMaxZoom=6 (the image only has 6 zoomify levels, a quirk of
; this map's own corpus script, not a SAS.Planet or port defect) - IntPower(2,nMaxZoom-zoom) is a
; NEGATIVE power (still exact, a fraction), so k<256 and the formula still evaluates to a large
; but well-defined nTileGroup, small enough to fit an S32; legacy behaviour reproduced as-is, not
; corrected.
;
; P4 (zoom=17): same shape as P3, but nTileGroup's arithmetic overflows 32 bits partway through,
; and the ENGINE and the PORT diverge on what happens next (docs/handoffs/T-0015D-review.md
; finding 1). k=256*IntPower(2,6-17)=0.125 (exact), mult:=Trunc(Ceil(9910/k))=Trunc(79280)=79280.
; GetTilesCount(17) = sum of GetTilesAtZoom(i), i=0..16 = 1,580,529,013 (re-derived independently
; by the reviewer; no intermediate partial sum crosses 2^31, so this sum itself never wraps).
; nTileGroup := (GetX + GetY*mult + GetTilesCount(zoom)) div 256 is where they diverge: in
; PascalScript, `Trunc` returns `LongInt` (uPSCompiler.pas:13571) and `GetY` is an S32 script
; variable (u_TileDownloadRequestBuilderPascalScriptVars.pas:143), so an S32*S32 product is
; computed and stored in an S32 temp (uPSRuntime.pas:6052) - every intermediate below wraps mod
; 2^32 (SAS.Planet is built with overflow checks off: no $Q+, no DCC_IntegerOverflowCheck):
;   GetY*mult   = 87654 * 79280        =  6,949,209,120  -> S32 wrap -> -1,640,725,472
;   + GetX      = -1,640,725,472 + 131,071               =    -1,640,594,401
;   + GetTilesCount(17) = -1,640,594,401 + 1,580,529,013  =       -60,065,388
;   div 256 (Pascal div truncates toward zero)            =          -234,630
; nTileGroup = -234630, so legacy's ResultURL ends .../TileGroup-234630/17-131071-87654.jpg. The
; port keeps integers as qint64 and wraps only on assignment (spec script.md §N1), so it computes
; the SAME expression without ever wrapping the S32 intermediates and gets a different, larger
; nTileGroup - that is the port's own integer model, not the engine's, and is wrong (PD-104,
; new). The golden below records the ENGINE's value (-234630), per the ticket rule that the hand
; derivation wins over the port when they disagree.
;
; PD-103 (port defect, see docs/handoffs/T-0015D.md): parser.cpp's parseConstSection() parsed a
; `const` declaration's value expression but never folded/stored it - the interpreter bound
; m_nWidth/m_nHeight to ordinary zero-initialised slots instead of 9910/7476, so every point below
; read them as 0 and diverged from this derivation. FIXED by T-0032 (Parser::foldConstExpr +
; CompiledScript::constValue/Interpreter::defaultValueForSlot) - see docs/handoffs/T-0032.md.
;
; PD-104 (port defect, see docs/handoffs/T-0015D-review.md): integer binary-op intermediates are
; computed in the operand's static 32-bit type by the engine but were never wrapped in the port's
; qint64 model (spec script.md §N1). Fixed by T-0031 (see docs/handoffs/T-0031.md). Every section
; below (P1-P4) is now asserted, not skipped.

